JavaScript Identifier Rules 🧠

Identifier basically kisi variable, function, object etc. ka naam hota hai.

Example:

let name = "Sania";

Yahan name identifier hai.

✅ Rules

1. Letters, digits, _ aur $ use kar sakte ho

let name = "Sania";
let age23 = 23;
let user_name = "Sania";
let $price = 500;

2. Identifier number se start nahi ho sakta ❌

let 123name = "Sania"; // ❌

Lekin number baad mein aa sakta hai:

let name123 = "Sania"; // ✅

3. Spaces allowed nahi hain ❌

let first name = "Sania"; // ❌

Instead:

let firstName = "Sania"; // ✅

4. Special characters allowed nahi hain ❌

let user-name = "Sania"; // ❌

- identifier ka part nahi ho sakta.

Use:

let userName = "Sania"; // ✅

5. JavaScript keywords use nahi kar sakte

let let = 10;       // ❌
let class = "A";    // ❌
let function = 20;  // ❌

Examples of keywords:

let, const, var, if, else, for, while, function, return, class etc.

6. JavaScript identifiers are case-sensitive ⭐

let name = "Sania";
let Name = "Anu";

